      "text": "To find the area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can apply the formula for the area of a triangle when we know the lengths of the base and height. The base of this triangle is the vertical distance between \\((0,0)\\) and \\((0,5)\\), which is 5 units. The height is the horizontal distance between these two points, which is 7 units. \n\nHere are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. Define the coordinates of the vertices of the triangle.\n2. Calculate the base and height.\n3. Use the formula \\(\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\\) to find the area.\n\nLet's compute this using Python:\n```python\n# Define the coordinates of the vertices\r\nbase = 5  # because it's the vertical distance between (0,0) and (0,5)\r\nheight = 7  # because it's the length of the horizontal distance between the points\r\n\r\n# Calculate the area using the formula\r\narea = 0.5 * base * height\r\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\( \\boxed{17.5} \\) square units.",
