      "text": "To find the area of a triangle with given vertices, we can use the formula known as Heron's formula. To use this formula, we first need to find the lengths of the sides of the triangle:\n\n$a = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$, where $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ are the coordinates of the two endpoints of the side. Here, $a$ represents the side length between $(0,0)$ and $(0,5)$. Similarly, we can compute the lengths of the other sides.\n\nThen, we apply Heron's formula to calculate the area:\n\n$area = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}$, where $s=\\frac{a+b+c}{2}$.\n\nLet's follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate $a$:\n$a = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{(0 - 0)^2 + (5 - 0)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{0 + 25}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{25}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = 5$\n\n2. Calculate $b$:\n$b = \\sqrt{(x_3 - x_2)^2 + (y_3 - y_2)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{(7 - 0)^2 + (12 - 5)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{49 + 49}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{98}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\approx 9.899$\n\n3. Calculate $c$:\n$c = \\sqrt{(x_3 - x_1)^2 + (y_3 - y_1)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{(7 - 0)^2 + (12 - 0)^2}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{49 + 144}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ = \\sqrt{193}$\n$\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\approx 13.891$\n\n4. Calculate the semi-perimeter $s$:\n$s = \\frac{a + b + c}{2}$\n$s = \\frac{5 + 9.899 + 13.891}{2}$\n$s \\approx 14.3995$\n\n5. Apply Heron's formula to find the area:\n$area = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}$\n$ \\approx \\sqrt{14.3995(14.3995-5)(14.3995-9.899)(14.3995-13.891)}$\n$ \\approx \\sqrt{14.3995(9.3995)(4.5)(0.5)}$\n$ \\approx 27.1$\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is approximately $\\boxed{27.1}$ square units.\nThe final answer is \\boxed{27.1}",
